#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Drive a hands-free tour of a live Umoja session and capture it.

Run it from a terminal inside an Umoja session, then keep your hands off the
keyboard and mouse until it says it is done (about three minutes). It opens a
few apps, walks through the app grid, the workspaces overview, Quick Settings,
notifications, the keyboard shortcuts guide, the screenshot UI, the
screensaver and the AI assistant (asked through the local model), and writes

    <out>/README.md        a tour page with every shot and clip
    <out>/snippet.md       a short gallery to paste into the top-level README
    <out>/images/*.png     stills (grim)
    <out>/videos/*.gif     short clips that GitHub plays inline (needs ffmpeg)
    <out>/videos/*.mp4     the same clips as H.264 (needs ffmpeg)

<out> defaults to docs/demo in this checkout, so `git add docs/demo` is all
that is left to do. See tools/demo/README.md for the options.

Everything is driven over Umoja's own D-Bus APIs (org.umoja.Overlay,
org.umoja.Panel, org.umoja.Compositor, org.freedesktop.Notifications); no
keyboard or mouse input is injected. While it runs it holds an idle
inhibitor, and before every step it checks that the screen is neither blanked
nor locked: if it is, the tour stops and only tidies up over D-Bus.
"""

